1
00:00:01,200 --> 00:00:06,760
The animals filed slowly past, and each gazed his fill.

2
00:00:06,760 --> 00:00:11,879
And Boxer put out his nose to sniff at the banknotes, and the flimsy white

3
00:00:11,879 --> 00:00:17,000
things stirred and rustled in his breath.

4
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:21,000
Three days later, there was a terrible hullabaloo.

5
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:26,760
Whymper, his face deadly pale, came racing up the path on his bicycle, flung

6
00:00:26,760 --> 00:00:31,239
it down in the yard, and rushed straight into the farmhouse.

7
00:00:31,239 --> 00:00:37,559
The next moment, a choking roar of rage sounded from Napoleon's apartments.

8
00:00:37,559 --> 00:00:41,879
The news of what had happened spread round the farm like wildfire.

9
00:00:41,879 --> 00:00:47,559
The banknotes were forgeries. Frederick had got the timber for nothing.

10
00:00:47,559 --> 00:00:52,319
Napoleon called the animals together immediately, and in a terrible voice

11
00:00:52,319 --> 00:00:56,040
pronounced the death sentence upon Frederick.

12
00:00:56,040 --> 00:01:01,159
"When captured," he said, "Frederick should be boiled alive."

13
00:01:01,159 --> 00:01:08,719
At the same time, he warned them that after this treacherous deed, the worst was to be expected.

14
00:01:08,719 --> 00:01:12,000
Frederick and his men might make their long-expected attack at any moment.
